sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Git as git push
    participant Hook as .git-hooks/pre-push
    participant Tool as tools/guarantees.py
    participant Server as staged test infrastructure

    Git->>Hook: one line per ref on stdin
    Hook->>Hook: keep every sha that is not a deletion<br/>and not already on the remote (HEAD when run by hand)
    Note over Hook: no commit sent, or tests_needed no → NOT RUN, and the push goes ahead
    Hook->>Hook: activate_venv, pytest present, duplicate code — unchanged
    Hook->>Hook: tools/guarantees.py or python missing → FAILED

    loop once per kept sha, one run per tree, stopping at a certain refusal
        Hook->>Tool: python -u tools/guarantees.py --ref sha
        Tool->>Tool: git archive sha into a temp tree
        Tool->>Server: runtime entry: staged here, or in the main checkout?
        alt staged
            Tool->>Tool: run the proofs, remove the guard, run them again
        else staged nowhere
            Note over Tool,Server: unmeasured
        end
        Tool-->>Hook: each result as it finishes, then the worst one's exit
    end

    Hook->>Hook: worst by rank, in the order RANK puts results
    alt unproved, broken, or an exit the tool does not name
        Hook-->>Git: FAILED — push refused
    else unmeasured at worst
        Hook->>Hook: PASSED WITH UNMEASURED GUARANTEES
    else all proved or exempt
        Hook->>Hook: ok
    end
    Hook->>Hook: any later checks the project wired in — each can still refuse
